    "body": "As long as there is nothing else racing with the resource fetch algorithm to read or write the state in question (`networkState`, the delaying-the-load-event flag, etc.) then I think there's no problem in principle. Any tasks to fire events that are queued will not have a reliable order with events originating from elsewhere, but that matches the reality that network timing is unreliable.\n\nThat being said, I suspect the way this algorithm is written isn't really a close match to any implementation. At least in Blink, the \"End the synchronous section\" before invoking the resource fetch algorithm doesn't actually show up in the code. Is there a mismatch here for Gecko/Servo too?\n",
